       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Amlodipine's maximum recommended dose is 10 mg once daily for adults. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. It might also be a typo for 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. I can't verify that this order was authorized, and I shouldn't enter it on a non-clinician's behalf.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves.\n- If the prescriber meant 5 mg or 10 mg, have them send me the corrected order. I can enter it once a clinician confirms it."
      }
