       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming it yourself doesn't give it clinical authorization. The order needs to come from a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose. It risks severe hypotension and circulatory collapse, and nothing in the patient's profile (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) justifies it.\n\nPlease contact the prescribing clinician or the pharmacist on the medicine service. If a clinician really intends a dose this far above the maximum, they should enter it themselves through the proper channels. Those channels include pharmacy verification and documented rationale. If the intended dose was 5 mg or 10 mg, the clinician can send me the corrected order and I'll enter it."
